{"additions":550,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPart of #148, closes #151.\n\n- A **Board-layout saved view** renders per its definition:\n  - **Columns** — `verticalGroupByFields` picks the column field (any single-select or iteration field): options in GitHub's order (kept even when empty), values the options no longer list, `No <field>` last. Unset falls back to `Status` (`columns_by`, which the classic kanban now also goes through).\n  - **Card order** — `sortByFields` orders the cards inside each column (shared `sort_items_dir`).\n  - **Swimlanes** — `groupByFields` renders one band per value: a header line (`▾ P1 (3)`) above the lane's own copy of the columns. `Space` collapses / expands the selected lane (`▸`) and the selection escapes to the nearest expanded lane; `j` / `k` cross into the neighbouring lane at a column's edge; a search jump into a collapsed lane expands it. Lanes scroll so the selected one always has room for at least one card; collapsed state survives a refresh (matched by lane name).\n- An ungrouped board is a single unnamed lane rendered exactly as before. The pane title notes a non-`Status` column field (`[columns: Priority]`) and the lane field (`· lanes: <field>`).\n\n## Docs / demo\n\n- Guide (en/ja) saved-views section describes the Board rendering; `Space` rows in the key tables (guide / README / Config Reference).\n- `tape/demo-projects.tape`: `v` now lands on the demo project's real Board-layout view (`By status`, header `· By status [board] (2/3)`); GIF re-recorded live.\n\n## Tests\n\nColumns from `verticalGroupByFields` (option order, empties kept, `No <field>`), lanes built per `groupByFields` with `j` crossing lanes / `Space` collapse escape / search-jump expansion, and view-sort ordering inside columns. 365 tests green, clippy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":11,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T06:11:00Z","deletions":73,"headRefName":"feat/projects-view-board","labels":[],"number":161,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMbA2xg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere is a confirmed layout bug risk due to truncating a potentially large `usize` into `u16` before clamping in the swimlane height calculation.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR extends the Projects page’s Board rendering to follow a saved view’s definition (column field via `verticalGroupByFields`, swimlanes via `groupByFields`, and card ordering via `sortByFields`), while keeping the feature read-only and updating docs/demo assets accordingly.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add swimlane support to the Projects board pane, including lane collapsing/expanding with `Space` and cross-lane navigation at column edges.\n- Generalize kanban column construction into a shared `columns_by(...)` helper driven by an arbitrary field (defaulting to `Status`).\n- Update default keybindings, docs (en/ja), and the Projects demo tape/GIF to reflect the new behavior.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-projects.tape | Updates the recorded demo interaction to switch to the next saved view (`v`). |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Implements board swimlanes, lane toggle action, lane-aware selection/scrolling, and view-driven board layout behavior. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Replaces the fixed Status-only column builder with a generalized `columns_by` helper used by board rendering. |\r\n| README.md | Documents `Space` binding for swimlane collapse/expand. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README key table update for `Space` swimlane toggle. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Expands guide text to describe Board view rendering rules and adds `Space` binding. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-reference.md | Adds `ToggleLane` (`Space`) to the Projects page config reference. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese guide update describing Board view behavior and `Space` binding. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md | Japanese config reference update for `ToggleLane` (`Space`). |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Updates the demo GIF (LFS pointer change). |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds the `Space` → `ToggleLane` binding for the Projects board pane. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 11/11 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T06:14:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"63d1c99c1bf5774fdd6d6f83107ae0728e8576ff"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMbD1rQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe board selection fallback after refresh can leave the selection on a collapsed swimlane in certain reordering/removal cases, making the selection effectively invisible until expanded.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**Previously missed (1)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/projects/panes/board.rs:295**\n* When a refresh can’t keep the selected item (`keep` not found), the fallback selection clamps `self.lane` but doesn’t ensure the resulting lane isn’t collapsed. If lane order changes (e.g., an earlier lane disappears) this can leave the selection inside a collapsed lane, making it effectively invisible until the user expands it. Consider moving the selection off a collapsed lane in this fallback path (consistent with the intended “selection escapes collapsed lanes” behavior).\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 11/11 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T06:22:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"46ea268d2cfd8533c23644920c22c7f4e2c514d1"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMbNR2w","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T06:44:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"46ea268d2cfd8533c23644920c22c7f4e2c514d1"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMbNSjA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T06:44:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"46ea268d2cfd8533c23644920c22c7f4e2c514d1"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T07:25:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34095364806/job/101657763725","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-07T07:25:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T06:20:28Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34090277466/job/101642166914","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:01Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:37Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34090277459/job/101642167159","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:03Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T06:20:13Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34090277466/job/101642167143","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:03Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T06:20:31Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34090277466/job/101642167142","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T06:20:31Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34090277466/job/101642497571","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-09-07T06:20:32Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T07:25:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34095364806/job/101657723289","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-09-07T07:25:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:52Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34090277459/job/101642167364","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:01Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T06:20:05Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34090277459/job/101642167352","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-07T06:19:04Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T07:25:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34095364806/job/101657723974","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-09-07T07:25:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Projects: Board layout with the view's column field and swimlanes"}
